      "text": "To solve the problem of finding \\( z \\) such that the projection of \\(\\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ z \\end{pmatrix}\\) onto \\(\\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\\) is \\(\\frac{12}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Projection Formula**:\n   The projection of vector \\(\\mathbf{v}\\) onto vector \\(\\mathbf{u}\\) is given by:\n   \\[\n   \\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{u}} \\mathbf{v} = \\frac{\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{v}}{\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{u}} \\mathbf{u}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Given Data**:\n   - Vector \\(\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ z \\end{pmatrix}\\)\n   - Vector \\(\\mathbf{u} = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\\)\n   - Projection: \\(\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{u}} \\mathbf{v} = \\frac{12}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\\)\n\n3. **Compute the Dot Products**:\n   - Calculate \\(\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{v}\\):\n     \\[\n     \\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{v} = (-3)(0) + (5)(3) + (-1)(z) = 15 - z\n     \\]\n   - Calculate \\(\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{u}\\):\n     \\[\n     \\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{u} = (-3)^2 + 5^2 + (-1)^2 = 9 + 25 + 1 = 35\n     \\]\n\n4. **Projection Expression**:\n   Using the projection formula:\n   \\[\n   \\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{u}} \\mathbf{v} = \\frac{15 - z}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Set Up the Equation**:\n   Given the projection is \\(\\frac{12}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\\), we equate:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{15 - z}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\frac{12}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n   \\]\n\n6. **Simplify the Equation**:\n   Since the vectors are proportional, we can equate the coefficients:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{15 - z}{35} = \\frac{12}{35}\n   \\]\n\n7. **Solve for \\( z \\)**:\n   \\[\n   15 - z = 12\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   z = 15 - 12\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   z = 3\n   \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( z \\) is \\(\\boxed{3}\\).",
