      "text": "To find the value of \\( z \\) such that the projection of the vector \\( \\mathbf{a} = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ z \\end{pmatrix} \\) onto the vector \\( \\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix} \\) is given by \\( \\frac{12}{35} \\mathbf{b} \\), we start by using the formula for the projection of \\( \\mathbf{a} \\) onto \\( \\mathbf{b} \\):\n\n\\[\n\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{a} = \\frac{\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}}{\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{b}\n\\]\n\nFirst, we compute the dot product \\( \\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} \\):\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ z \\end{pmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix} = 0 \\cdot (-3) + 3 \\cdot 5 + z \\cdot (-1) = 15 - z\n\\]\n\nNext, we compute the dot product \\( \\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} \\):\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix} = (-3)^2 + 5^2 + (-1)^2 = 9 + 25 + 1 = 35\n\\]\n\nSubstituting these into the projection formula, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{a} = \\frac{15 - z}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nWe are given that this projection is equal to \\( \\frac{12}{35} \\mathbf{b} \\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{15 - z}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\frac{12}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{15 - z}{35} = \\frac{12}{35}\n\\]\n\nBy equating the numerators, we get:\n\n\\[\n15 - z = 12\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\( z \\), we find:\n\n\\[\nz = 15 - 12 = 3\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( z \\) is \\(\\boxed{3}\\).",
